menu "OpenShock LED drivers"

    config OPENSHOCK_RGB_LED_DITHERING
        bool "10-bit dithering on the RGB LED"
        default y
        help
            The WS2812B takes 8 bits per color. With dithering the driver shows 10: it sends
            4 frames that each round a channel to one of the two nearest 8-bit levels, and the
            RMT hardware repeats them on its own while the color holds, so the average lands
            on the quarter step in between at no CPU cost.

            The looped frames need several RMT memory blocks. Chips without a transmit channel
            to spare for the RF transmitter after that (ESP32-C3) round to 8 bits regardless.

            Off, each color is rounded to the nearest 8-bit level.

endmenu
